cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or reference this architecture in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "octopus-brain: An Event-Triggered Modular Neural Architecture with Sparse Central Coalition Consolidation"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-27
license: MIT
authors:
  - name: "octopus-brain contributors"
abstract: >-
  An open-source research architecture inspired by cephalopod neuroanatomy,
  designed to investigate two specific hypotheses: (1) event-triggered asynchronous
  local-to-central communication with no global clock, and (2) dynamic, temporary coalition
  binding among peripheral processing modules that dissolves after execution.
keywords:
  - modular neural networks
  - distributed control
  - event-triggered communication
  - coalition attention
  - neuromorphic computing
  - multi-agent reinforcement learning
